load @term/seed/structure/space/hilbert
  find hilbert-space

# A Hermitian adjoint: the conjugate-transpose of an operator on an inner-product space, the operator that moves to the
# other side of the inner product. An operator equal to its own adjoint is self-adjoint (Hermitian), and such operators
# have real eigenvalues, which is why the observables of quantum mechanics are Hermitian. The form carries the Hilbert
# space the operator and its adjoint act on.
form hermitian-adjoint
  link space, like hilbert-space
